 ### Conditional InnerShell Emission
-This variant (VXL-046) defines the visibility rule for innerShell polygons. It states that innerShell emission does not depend on the presence or visibility of the outerShell in the current cell. Instead, it depends on the complete opaque closure of the six boundaries by neighboring cells. An isolated Shape without outerShell retains its innerShell. However, a Shape enclosed by six neighbors that are fully opaque omits its innerShell during the bake process [S1].
+This variant (VXL-046) defines the visibility rule for innerShell polygons [S1]. It states that innerShell emission does not depend on the presence or visibility of the outerShell in the current cell [S1]. Instead, it depends on the complete opaque closure of the six boundaries by neighboring cells [S1]. An isolated Shape without outerShell retains its innerShell [S1]. However, a Shape enclosed by six neighbors that are fully opaque omits its innerShell during the bake process [S1].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of polygons for classification. Mask generation is proportional to the area of the $1000 \times 1000$ grid, optimized by AABB unions.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for six $1000 \times 1000$ masks and the list of innerShell polygons.
-*   **Strengths:** Reduces boundary occlusion noise by ignoring non-coplanar interior geometry. Optimizes rendering by conditionally emitting innerShell geometry based on neighbor occlusion.
